{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods","id":1378119,"title":"Missing Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-02T17:52:25-07:00","id":1378119,"title":"Missing Gods","content":"What it says on the tin. Gods that we want to see show up later.<br /> <br /> I'm glad the Loa are promised. The Baron was particularly missed.<br /> <br /> For the Theoi four stand out. Hercules, who had more temples in ancient Greece/Hellas than several of the standard twelve and was a major deity in ancient times. Hecate, again a major figure. Iris, also a messenger of the gods. And the Roman god Mars, who is nothing like Ares. In fact Ares was rarely worshiped in Greece and Mars was a major figure in Rome. Ares was the god of battle lust and Mars was the god of adult male social roles. For early Rome these were Farmer, Solider, Priest, and husband/lover. The Solider role got overemphasized in the later empire.<br /> <br /> For the Tuatha, certain figured associated with their pantheon like Oberon and Mab who aren't true members but connected would be good.<br /> <br /> More as I think of them.<br /> <br /> Who do you want to show up later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:24:15-07:00","id":1378130,"title":"","content":"Yeah it seemed odd to me that Heracles arguably the most well known Greek God (Well him or Zeus) is absent in the core.<br /> But agree with your sentiments<br /> I would like Eos Goddess of the Dawn and Pan included. As well I would like Morpheus and Eros (I forgot it again if he was added yet), and I think they treated Thanatos and Hypnos as titans but they would be interesting.<br /> Kratos, Nike, Bia and Zelus would be interesting parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> Was Bragi included yet with the Aesir? I know in 1st ed they added him later. Maybe have rules for being the Child of a Valkyrie, and thus being in name and possibly in blood a grandchild of Odin.<br /> It would be interesting to introduce the two other brothers of Odin, Vili and Ve, and Hoenir. We have so little to go on so they could be interesting maybe instead as NPCs, I've toyed with the idea of fleshing out Vili and Ve as lost gods.<br /> <br /> I would be curious adding Santeria and Voudoun. And comparing relationships with say Papa Ghede and Baron Samedi and the other Baron Loa like Baron Cimetiere.<br /> <br /> The 8 Immortals though maybe they would adopt and uplift mortals into Heroes.<br /> <br /> And maybe now Weyland the Smith and Daedalus the inventor are Gods able to take Scions, because it would be hella cool to be a Scion of one of them. Didn't they mention something about Zhuge Liang being made into a god, or did I just imagine that.<br /> <br /> The Seven gods of Fortune for the Kami. They Added Inari already right? <br /> <br /> Rudra father of the Maruts, maybe as an aspect of Shiva or separate.<br /> <br /> And maybe treat Oberon, Titania and Queen Mab as Minor Gods of Elves, as in maybe Sidhe and Alfar mixing into a general European elf population.<br /> Mine as well toss in Morgan le fay into this, maybe as a Demigod if you don't want her a full god.<br /> <br /> I would treat the 4 Divine beasts as another cross Pantheon set of asian gods, the Vermilion Sparrow, the Blue Dragon, the Black Tortoise, and the White Tiger.<br /> Before in 1st ed I had a subgroup of divine Beasts/Pets taking human scions, so Sleipnir, Garm, Huninn, Muninn, Freki, Geri, and Cerberus but that is not for everyone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:04:24-07:00","id":1378141,"title":"","content":"Oberon and Mab aren't Irish. They're from a Shakespeare play. A Shakespeare play about a bunch of silly mortals that actually took place in Greece. If you want to add Tuatha there's a bunch of other figures who'd be so much more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Last I heard, Hecate's going to be in the Companion. Each Core Pantheon is gonna get a new Patron written up for the Companion.<br /> <br /> Hercules, I think, is going to be in Demigod. As will, last I heard, Weyland the Smith.<br /> <br /> It may be a good idea to try and separate Ares and Mars into very different Mantles, given the connotations to the two of them, yeah. Give Ares the Chaos, Passion, and War Purviews while Mars can have the Fertility, Prosperity, and War Purview, maybe with Passion (Valor).<br /> <br /> And of course if you're willing to put in some research, writing a God that you think got overlooked is pretty easy. I do get the &quot;The reason I pay for these books is so that I don't have to do research&quot; thing, but if further books come out and they don't have your favorite Kami you can hit up some sources, pick some Callings, and some Purviews.<br /> <br /> As for which Gods I hope to see... Fuck, I'unno. I'm always happy with more. My blind spots are such that I don't even know how much I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:18:37-07:00","id":1378144,"title":"","content":"I know they are from Shakespeare I'm proposing the likely origins of them. Just like how they had the Danish Prince a Scion of Vidar. I know they aren't Irish, I mentioned them in the same breath I was mentioning an Arthurian character like Morgan Lefay. I was incorporating nonmythological figures using mythology as a background because it seemed appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit<br /> <br /> And I don't know if I would give Ares Chaos. He doesn't have the Order of Athena but he is more about merciless slaughter then chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  added ares stuff 04-02-2020, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:31:05-07:00","id":1378148,"title":"","content":"I mean if they <i>don't</i> have a mythic backing, why give them one? Sometimes a Being can... BE without needing to be in a Pantheon or be called a God when they're not a God.<br /> <br /> Like, let's not do a 1e Yankee Pantheon here.<br /> <br /> Morgan Lefay also, I'd make a Sorcerer tentatively, rather than a God. Probably Demigod tier, but I'm just guessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:37:56-07:00","id":1378154,"title":"","content":"Really your comparing Oberon to Johnny Appleseed?<br /> Beowulf isn't mythology but we include that story in Scion with Beowulf as a Scion, and they talk about Caine's get but they put asterisks in it.<br /> <br /> If its not your cup of tea then ignore that bit of my post, but I just tossed it in there as suggestions. Do I need like a Scion club ticket to have an opinion?<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of how they made Hamleth a Scion, and they made the Earl King a Trollish being.<br /> <br /> Morgan LeFay probably wouldn't be God level she would be tied to faeries. Oberon and Titania would be immortal Royalty so they wouldn't need to be gods either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:48:11-07:00","id":1378158,"title":"","content":"You don't need anything to have an opinion, just like I don't need anything to have an opinion of &quot;I'd rather allocate the wordcount to other things like these-&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, Morgan I'd probably do something as a Sorcerer who learned mystic secrets from the Fae, assuming that there'll be mechanics for &quot;I have learned Secret Magics from something that is Not A God&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:34:09-07:00","id":1378166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378158#post1378158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need anything to have an opinion, just like I don't need anything to have an opinion of &quot;I'd rather allocate the wordcount to other things like these-&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, Morgan I'd probably do something as a Sorcerer who learned mystic secrets from the Fae, assuming that there'll be mechanics for &quot;I have learned Secret Magics from something that is Not A God&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How totalitarian.<br /> <br /> But the implication in the stories Merlin and Morgan both have magics from faery lineage. I would justify her magics the same way I would justify the various Faery beings already presented. I don't need to spoonfed a line explaining faeries give you this, this and this but not that. I could treat her as a less Divine Circes and I would be in a decent ballpark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:06:20-07:00","id":1378230,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d like to see the monotheistic \u2018pantheons\u2019 brought into the game. Obviously, not \u2018God\u2019 or \u2018Allah\u2019 directly, but the Angels and Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:25:59-07:00","id":1378233,"title":"","content":"Well, the Orishas are a Monotheist pantheon, and the Orishas themselves are not gods but spirits that are closer to god than we are, like angels and demons.<br /> <br /> A real Monotheist pantheon (a monotheon? Or would it be a Theo?) should be one god with a lot of purviews, and possibly a bunch of demigods (as the Middle Earth Pantheon, with Valar as Demigods and Maiar as Heroes, or Valar as gods and Maiar as Demigods following the Orisha naming).<br /> <br /> When you talk about angels and demons, you are automatically talking about Abrahanic god (God, Jave, Allah, etc), because they are part of that myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:32:41-07:00","id":1378235,"title":"","content":"If I was more up on my Shakespeare, I'd be tempted to try and write an adventure set in 16th century England involving the Bard and a trio of Scion Hero npcs who are clearly meant to be Oberon, Titania, and Puck, trying to reach Demigod status. <br /> <br /> As it is, the Theoi and Aesir are the ones I'm most familiar with, and there are a number of minor Greek and Roman ones I'd enjoy seeing in a modern context. Nike and Hebe spring immediately to mind. <br /> I'm very eager to see the new Loa, not just because they are another one I am more familiar with, but also they are the major example of an existing pantheon (the Orisha) shifting into something different from historical/cultural/geographic shifts, and I'm curious to learn how this works in the game and how I might possibly be able to apply it to the Theoi if I decided I wanted to do a full on Roman shift to them.<br /> <br /> I'm also really hoping that theoretical Welsh pantheon/King Arthur book becomes a real thing, because it sounds really cool, with a lot of potential for historical and modern games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:33:07-07:00","id":1378236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378141#post1378141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oberon and Mab aren't Irish. They're from a Shakespeare play. A Shakespeare play about a bunch of silly mortals that actually took place in Greece. If you want to add Tuatha there's a bunch of other figures who'd be so much more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Last I heard, Hecate's going to be in the Companion. Each Core Pantheon is gonna get a new Patron written up for the Companion.<br /> <br /> Hercules, I think, is going to be in Demigod. As will, last I heard, Weyland the Smith.<br /> <br /> It may be a good idea to try and separate Ares and Mars into very different Mantles, given the connotations to the two of them, yeah. Give Ares the Chaos, Passion, and War Purviews while Mars can have the Fertility, Prosperity, and War Purview, maybe with Passion (Valor).<br /> <br /> And of course if you're willing to put in some research, writing a God that you think got overlooked is pretty easy. I do get the &amp;quot;The reason I pay for these books is so that I don't have to do research&amp;quot; thing, but if further books come out and they don't have your favorite Kami you can hit up some sources, pick some Callings, and some Purviews.<br /> <br /> As for which Gods I hope to see... Fuck, I'unno. I'm always happy with more. My blind spots are such that I don't even know how much I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Oberon and Mab predate Shakespeare by centuries. Mab is a form of Meave (sic) and is Irish. There is debate about Oberon. And I did say they were associated not part of the Tautha.<br /> <br /> As for Hercules. The ancient Greeks and Romans worshiped him more widely than they worshiped Hera, Ares, or Hephaestus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:41:08-07:00","id":1378238,"title":"","content":"Eldagusto, I strongly agree about adding Baron Cimetiere, Pan (the traditional one), Eos, Morpheus, and Eos. The Roman gods Janus, Neptune (a god of springs and subterranean waters), Flora, Minerva (a goddess of skill and crafts), and Mercury (a god of markets and transit as opposed to comunication and travel, certainly Mercury was never a guide of dead souls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:43:00-07:00","id":1378240,"title":"","content":"With Herakles, I suspect the fact that he is one of Western mythology's most famous examples of a &quot;mortal&quot; hero ascending to divine status may have led to the design decision to wait until Demigod to detail him so that he could be more fully explored in the game's concept of crossing that threshold without any risk of possibly contradicting what might have been said in Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:46:20-07:00","id":1378241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378144#post1378144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know they are from Shakespeare I'm proposing the likely origins of them. Just like how they had the Danish Prince a Scion of Vidar. I know they aren't Irish, I mentioned them in the same breath I was mentioning an Arthurian character like Morgan Lefay. I was incorporating nonmythological figures using mythology as a background because it seemed appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit<br /> <br /> And I don't know if I would give Ares Chaos. He doesn't have the Order of Athena but he is more about merciless slaughter then chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Morgan le Fay and Merlin were described by Medieval authors as being &quot;Worshiped as Gods by simple folk back then.&quot; More than a few Arthurian scholars assume they're both gods that have been changed to mortals in legends. Some, far fewer, say this of Arthur. Certainly Joseph Campbell wasn't the only one who thought Arthur's tale was blended with that of old gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T08:31:55-07:00","id":1378273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378230#post1378230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d like to see the monotheistic \u2018pantheons\u2019 brought into the game. Obviously, not \u2018God\u2019 or \u2018Allah\u2019 directly, but the Angels and Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn\u2019t \u201ca\u201d monotheistic pantheon. There are many monotheistic belief systems. If you mean Abrahamic, say Abrahamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T08:57:48-07:00","id":1378278,"title":"","content":"We're getting Masks of the Mythos and Dragons, both of which spin Scion in entirely different directions than the core line. Perhaps we could also get a book that's less about gods and more about fables? That could handle the likes of Oberon and Titania, Santa Claus and Jack Frost, Paul Bunyan and John Henry. And I think the biggest mistake of 1e's Yankees (aside from trying to force them into the same setting as the Dodekatheon et al) was making all of them God-like: most should be Heroes, some should be counterparts to Demi-Gods, and a rare few should be God-tier. <br /> <br /> That would also be a place to try out the \u201cgods are dependent on mortal worshippers\u201d notion that Scion itself explicitly <i>doesn't</i> use but which is so prevalent among portions of the fanbase: the fables exist because people \u201cbelieve\u201d in them (for some definition of \u201cbelieve\u201d).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:08:01-07:00","id":1378280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378230#post1378230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d like to see the monotheistic \u2018pantheons\u2019 brought into the game. Obviously, not \u2018God\u2019 or \u2018Allah\u2019 directly, but the Angels and Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orisha are actually already in the game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> as are the Deva, several of whose traditions are Monotheistic (including mine)... the Yazata who are similar are coming in Companion.<br /> <br /> If you meant to say Abrahamic, then you're in luck since the the Tuatha De are all descended from Noah, so they fall into Abrahamic Cosmology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378130#post1378130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be curious adding Santeria and Voudoun. And comparing relationships with say Papa Ghede and Baron Samedi and the other Baron Loa like Baron Cimetiere.<br /> <br /> The Seven gods of Fortune for the Kami. They Added Inari already right?<br /> <br /> Rudra father of the Maruts, maybe as an aspect of Shiva or separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Loa are coming in Companion.<br /> <br /> All Seven Gods of Fortune are in the core.<br /> <br /> Puranic Rudra is so thoroughly absorbed into Shiva that a separate aspect would be difficult... Vedic era Rudra is an entirely different God with many interesting associations and attributes, but I feel that the Vedic Gods are more than different enough from the Puranic era ones to be their own separate Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378236#post1378236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Hercules. The ancient Greeks and Romans worshiped him more widely than they worshiped Hera, Ares, or Hephaestus.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGood thing he's coming in Demigod then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:34:16-07:00","id":1378287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378280#post1378280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Orisha are actually already in the game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> as are the Deva, several of whose traditions are Monotheistic (including mine)... the Yazata who are similar are coming in Companion.<br /> <br /> If you meant to say Abrahamic, then you're in luck since the the Tuatha De are all descended from Noah, so they fall into Abrahamic Cosmology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Loa are coming in Companion.<br /> <br /> All Seven Gods of Fortune are in the core.<br /> <br /> Puranic Rudra is so thoroughly absorbed into Shiva that a separate aspect would be difficult... Vedic era Rudra is an entirely different God with many interesting associations and attributes, but I feel that the Vedic Gods are more than different enough from the Puranic era ones to be their own separate Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bGood thing he's coming in Demigod then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>See I always mix up 1st ed and 2nd. :P<br /> <br /> You don't think they would be a sub Pantheon like the Loa or the Roman Pantheon (pantheon of mantles I guess) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:36:25-07:00","id":1378290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378287#post1378287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See I always mix up 1st ed and 2nd. :P<br /> <br /> You don't think they would be a sub Pantheon like the Loa or the Roman Pantheon (pantheon of mantles I guess) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can they be? Yes. Would they be *better* as a separate one? Also Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:40:01-07:00","id":1378292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378290#post1378290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can they be? Yes. Would they be *better* as a separate one? Also Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be of the opinion the Loa too would have been better? I know some have shared that sentiment. I'm fine either way. I was one of the ones who made stink over Sekhmet shouldn't have just been Bast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:49:32-07:00","id":1378295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378292#post1378292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you be of the opinion the Loa too would have been better? I know some have shared that sentiment. I'm fine either way. I was one of the ones who made stink over Sekhmet shouldn't have just been Bast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about the Loa or Orisha to make that call <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am a one trick pony, my area of expertise are the Hindu Pantheon and their predecessors, the Vedic one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:22:07-07:00","id":1378324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378166#post1378166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How totalitarian.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>That's not respectful towards the poster or the conversation. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:02:17-07:00","id":1378342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378324#post1378324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>That's not respectful towards the poster or the conversation. </b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I dispute this, you will punish me for disputing this. There is no method of disputing moderation when moderators handle the complaints. I've pointed out disagreements with you in the past and my opinion of you misusing your power because you have an arbitrary grudge. You will ban me and there will be no consequence to your history of behavior.<br /> <br /> I was responding to someone's response that I interpreted as they don't respect anyone who disagrees with them. The starter of the conversation even rebutted with validation for my opinion.<br /> <br /> Once again Lioness In my opinion is going to abuse their power to pursue a grudge. There is no mediation or a system for pursuing redress. Civility was upheld even in this very post I am making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:53:22-07:00","id":1378366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dispute this, you will punish me for disputing this. There is no method of disputing moderation when moderators handle the complaints. </div> </div> </div> There <i>is</i> a way of disputing moderation: you can Flag the moderator's warning post, which subjects it to review by the moderators (presumably including the other ones). That keeps it off-forum, which is in general why the moderators discourage discussion of their decisions <i>on</i> forum, and potentially lets other moderators who may have a different opinion get involved, or not, as they see fit \u2014 which wouldn't happen if you just send a private message to the moderator. <br /> <br /> And that's all I have to say about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:58:55-07:00","id":1378367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378295#post1378295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know enough about the Loa or Orisha to make that call <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am a one trick pony, my area of expertise are the Hindu Pantheon and their predecessors, the Vedic one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any opinions on new Deva that would be fun or interesting to include in future material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:26:52-07:00","id":1378371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378367#post1378367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any opinions on new Deva that would be fun or interesting to include in future material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have one I wrote up ages ago for free <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Ganga, Whose Waters Cleanse the Worlds</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <b>Aliases:</b> Bhagirathi, Alaknanda, Surtarangini<br /> <br /> Praise be to Ganga, Goddess of the sacred waters that flow through the realms of Deva, Human and Asura alike. When Vishnu in his Dwarf Incarnation raised his foot to cover all Heaven, his toe pierced the Primordial Waters, and a stream shot forth, bathing his feet, before being collected by Brahma in his water-pot. This selfsame stream is Ganga, daughter of the Himalaya Mountains and sister to Parvati.<br /> <br /> Bhagiratha, Scion of Shiva, born through his blessing to two Queens, sought to bring Ganga down to Earth, as a means of salvation for his cursed ancestors. Pleased with his austerities, Brahma tipped over his water-pot, and Ganga raced towards the World; but in her arrogance, Ganga thought to smash through the ground. Fearing that he had doomed humanity, Bhagiratha invoked Shiva, who answered his call. Shiva stood at the point of impact, and caught Ganga up in his matted locks, before letting her loose in a controlled stream. Bhagiratha then worshipped her and explained his mission, to help all humanity with her waters.<br /> <br /> This experience changed Ganga, who took Bhagirath's name as one of her own; she spread her waters out into all realms of existence, existing as a river in Heaven Earth and Hell, and other regions besides, and now dedicates herself to the salvation of Deva, Human and Asura alike. Like Ganesha, she is an advocate of peace, and her many children usually inherit their mother's altruistic streak. With King Santanu, Ganga bore the mightiest of Born Deva Scions, Bheeshma of the Mahabharata. She often takes an active role in her Scions' development, and they likewise spearhead efforts to purify her sacred river. Still, some of them fear that they will never live up to their most famous sibling.<br /> <br /> <i>Callings:</i> <br /> \u2022 <i>Healer:</i> Strongly associated with purification and the salvation of souls<br /> \u2022 <i>Liminal:</i> Her flows exist in multiple realms simultaneously, capable of releasing souls and sending them to their next destination<br /> \u2022 <i>Lover:</i> Seduces King Santanu, is often linked to multiple Gods with no clear consensus on a husband<br /> <br /> Purviews: <br /> \u2022 <i>Fertility:</i> Mother Goddess prayed to for fertile fields, considered spiritual mother by many along her banks<br /> \u2022 <i>Journeys:</i> Moves between Worlds with ease, her waters allow passage to other Terrae<br /> \u2022 <i>Water:</i> Most famous of the river Goddesses of India","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:30:30-07:00","id":1378374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378366#post1378366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There <i>is</i> a way of disputing moderation: you can Flag the moderator's warning post, which subjects it to review by the moderators (presumably including the other ones). That keeps it off-forum, which is in general why the moderators discourage discussion of their decisions <i>on</i> forum, and potentially lets other moderators who may have a different opinion get involved, or not, as they see fit \u2014 which wouldn't happen if you just send a private message to the moderator.<br /> <br /> And that's all I have to say about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're able to appeal directly to the Forum Administration by &quot;the Contact Us&quot; option on the bottom of the page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:31:51-07:00","id":1378375,"title":"","content":"That aside, I think the Ashvin Twins are ok candidates... they are much less Legendary than their Vedic counterparts, but are fathers to two of the Pandava brothers... I believe Vishvvakarma the Craftsman God will be coming in Companion, so there's another one covered... and I'm well-known to have a soft spot for Santoshi, Goddess of Satisfaction, Daughter of Ganesha, whose Deeds were first told to the World via a 1960's Bollywood movie <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:46:04-07:00","id":1378379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378273#post1378273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There isn\u2019t \u201ca\u201d monotheistic pantheon. There are many monotheistic belief systems. If you mean Abrahamic, say Abrahamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a ridiculously pedantic post!<br /> <br /> I was just making a single suggestion. Yes, I was referring to Abrahamic religions in the main, but if people have suggestions following on of other monotheism religions that is fine also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:04:01-07:00","id":1378387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378379#post1378379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What a ridiculously pedantic post!<br /> <br /> I was just making a single suggestion. Yes, I was referring to Abrahamic religions in the main, but if people have suggestions following on of other monotheism religions that is fine also.</div> </div> </div> </div>there are a few Abrahanic pantheons around if you deep dive in the posts. Most of them are from when the backers received the first version of the book with proper formatting, so they must be really down the list. You can find (probably) by searching for the archangels names, but I may be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:43:54-07:00","id":1378414,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure we're not going to get official versions of them, though. <i>Maybe</i> something in the Nexus from a suitably enterprising fan, assuming the guidelines permit it; but nothing from Onyx Path themselves. Too much of a hot potato. <br /> <br /> I could be wrong, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:51:26-07:00","id":1378417,"title":"","content":"I haven't heard anything about Onyx Path doing anything official for the Abrahamic Religions, no. I've heard grousing here and there about doing a Canaanite Pantheon, and if they do they'll probably have to address that yes the Abrahamic Religions exist in Scion (more explicitly than they already have at least).<br /> <br /> Again, that was just Hmm-ing and Haw-ing, and wishfully going &quot;It'd be cool if-&quot; rather than anything confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:07:45-07:00","id":1378424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378417#post1378417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't heard anything about Onyx Path doing anything official for the Abrahamic Religions, no. I've heard grousing here and there about doing a Canaanite Pantheon, and if they do they'll probably have to address that yes the Abrahamic Religions exist in Scion (more explicitly than they already have at least).<br /> <br /> Again, that was just Hmm-ing and Haw-ing, and wishfully going &quot;It'd be cool if-&quot; rather than anything confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think it would make for a great conflict in the game, is all. In the same way that, in American Gods, the narrative is built on a conflict between the 'Old Gods' and the \u2018New Gods\u2019. Having an external threat to allow the different pantheons want to work together, gives a good overarching narrative device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:08:52-07:00","id":1378425,"title":"","content":"I'd kind of like to see a Phoenician/Carthaginian Pantheon at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:11:25-07:00","id":1378427,"title":"","content":"I think the Abrahanic pantheon is not going to be in any official book, neither it\u2019s going to be in any Nexus (for longer than it takes for OPP check it. I may be wrong but I am quite sure there is a restriction on Monotheistic religions in the Nexus and OPP in general (to avoid a bunch of Karens after Rich).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:11:31-07:00","id":1378428,"title":"","content":"Also, I am toying with the idea of making a Trinity/Scion crossover...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T19:14:41-07:00","id":1378450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378428#post1378428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I am toying with the idea of making a Trinity/Scion crossover...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was always trying to set up a Scion 1st e /Mage the Ascension crossover. But my gaming groups kept collapsing on me. Sigh!<br /> <br /> I had one game were certain gods used paradox to turn Mages into Scions for neferious purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-03-2020, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T22:11:11-07:00","id":1378472,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I'd be interested in a supplement for Scion that focuses on sorcerers. Nearly all of the crunch is already there in the form of Motifs and Purviews; so instead of focusing on that side of things, I'd rather see a focus on how one becomes a Sorcerer, coupled with an overview of magical traditions that exist in the World, what they're like, and how they're connected to the Pantheons. Done with the same respect toward the corresponding real-world magical beliefs that Scion has shown toward the religious beliefs that the Pantheons represent. <br /> <br /> In short, Scion really ought to have its own mages, without needing to borrow them from the World or Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T23:30:08-07:00","id":1378476,"title":"","content":"Writing an entire RPG about how religions and mythologies are real without a plan to include the Judeo-christian religions at some point would be a baffling and disappointing decision to me to be honest. It would be like writing an RPG set in 1st century Europe and barely even mention the Roman empire but just continually fleshing out all the other contemporary cultures and civilizations inside and outside of it.<br /> <br /> Also I agree with Dataweaver, it would be very interesting to see a deep dive into sorcerers and various magical cultures. Give more options for those of us who sometimes want to play more low-fantasy and low-power games of Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 04-04-2020, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T23:48:31-07:00","id":1378478,"title":"","content":"I agree with all this. I just think that the basic premise of Scion is a gem - and can really be expanded out with all these other groups added in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T02:03:57-07:00","id":1378489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378476#post1378476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writing an entire RPG about how religions and mythologies are real without a plan to include the Judeo-christian religions at some point would be a baffling and disappointing decision to me to be honest. It would be like writing an RPG set in 1st century Europe and barely even mention the Roman empire but just continually fleshing out all the other contemporary cultures and civilizations inside and outside of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely understand the hesitation to go into it, because turns out Judeism, Christianity, and Islam aren't very easy to write up in one concise write-up. Last I've heard whispers of, it's a case of &quot;If we do this we want to do it carefully and right&quot;, but I can only really repeat what I've heard; I'm not actually working for OPP. And if I were... Fuck, I wouldn't know where to start with trying to write up an actual Christian-based Pantheon. Do I use the Angels as Patrons? Do I use the Catholic Saints? Why Catholicism? Where does Lutheran or Baptist beliefs fit? Fuck me, I'm not sure WHERE to begin. I'm not good enough for that, and it'd take a lot of research to do that.<br /> <br /> Until then, I'm running them at my table as &quot;They exist and are as real as the other religions, if you want to talk about them we may tap some fan supplements&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Many People</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerer Supplement</div> </div> </div> </div>I wager one's in production. I dunno, maybe it'll be in Saints and Monsters, if that's focusing on Saints and other non-Scion Denizens as I assume it is. I even saw earlier drafts from the Kickstarter which had some attempted Sorcerer Paths, but those got pulled so that Sorcerers could get a more extensive rework. So yeah, More Sorcerer Support is definitely something I assume is coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T02:06:13-07:00","id":1378490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378472#post1378472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I'd be interested in a supplement for Scion that focuses on sorcerers. Nearly all of the crunch is already there in the form of Motifs and Purviews; so instead of focusing on that side of things, I'd rather see a focus on how one becomes a Sorcerer, coupled with an overview of magical traditions that exist in the World, what they're like, and how they're connected to the Pantheons. Done with the same respect toward the corresponding real-world magical beliefs that Scion has shown toward the religious beliefs that the Pantheons represent.<br /> <br /> In short, Scion really ought to have its own mages, without needing to borrow them from the World or Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the best of all possible worlds, I like to imagine each pantheon having its own sourcebook somewhere between the size of Origin and Hero that includes an entire chapter about sorcerers/magicians/whathaveyou in the context of that pantheon's religion, culture and history (as well as ones about supernatural races, terra incognita, divine realms, and so forth). But as is, I'd be ecstatic to see a sorcerers book like what you describe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T02:56:33-07:00","id":1378492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378489#post1378489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely understand the hesitation to go into it, because turns out Judeism, Christianity, and Islam aren't very easy to write up in one concise write-up. Last I've heard whispers of, it's a case of &quot;If we do this we want to do it carefully and right&quot;, but I can only really repeat what I've heard; I'm not actually working for OPP. And if I were... Fuck, I wouldn't know where to start with trying to write up an actual Christian-based Pantheon. Do I use the Angels as Patrons? Do I use the Catholic Saints? Why Catholicism? Where does Lutheran or Baptist beliefs fit? Fuck me, I'm not sure WHERE to begin. I'm not good enough for that, and it'd take a lot of research to do that.<br /> <br /> Until then, I'm running them at my table as &quot;They exist and are as real as the other religions, if you want to talk about them we may tap some fan supplements&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wager one's in production. I dunno, maybe it'll be in Saints and Monsters, if that's focusing on Saints and other non-Scion Denizens as I assume it is. I even saw earlier drafts from the Kickstarter which had some attempted Sorcerer Paths, but those got pulled so that Sorcerers could get a more extensive rework. So yeah, More Sorcerer Support is definitely something I assume is coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it\u2019s worth noting that other games have managed to do this, although I accept that they need to be mindful of real world religious groups. I wouldn\u2019t say that these religious backgrounds are necessarily more complex that the religious pantheons outlined in the game already though. They are just a bit more proximal in the current age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T05:53:19-07:00","id":1378509,"title":"","content":"Well... writing about Abrahanic myths (mostly about Christian myths) will have an immediate bad feedback. The reason is, the Christianity in the book is about love and tolerance, but the followers use it to hate and prejudice. Writing a book about how Cristian myths are equal to pagan myths will bring an unproductive attention to the game and publisher.<br /> <br /> I said once, and will say again, the religion groups that were pointed in the book are: 1. Virtually dead religions; or 2. Already treated as second class religions in US (where OPP is based).<br /> The people that practice these religions are used to be portrayed as believing in fairy tales or satanists or whatever. Their religions are their religions, what they believe is what they believe, they don\u2019t expect you believe in it too. Christians are not used to be treated like this, for example, in their minds even if you don\u2019t believe in their religion you still need to be afraid of hell (more than once I heard \u201cYou don\u2019t believe in Jesus? You know you are going to hell for that don\u2019t you?\u201d) just because in their minds their myths are real and unquestionable.<br /> <br /> Tl;DR: Don\u2019t ask for Abrahanic supplement in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-04-2020, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:03:51-07:00","id":1378512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378509#post1378509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... writing about Abrahanic myths (mostly about Christian myths) will have an immediate bad feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf games have been offending certain Christian groups since they were founded. Vampire\u2019s lore is based on Christian myths. I doubt it will make any difference here, truth be told.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:13:11-07:00","id":1378515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378512#post1378512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf games have been offending certain Christian groups since they were founded. Vampire\u2019s lore is based on Christian myths. I doubt it will make any difference here, truth be told.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but they were in the first case attacking the followers and not the beliefs system and in the second case starting the entire premises that Christian myths are true.<br /> When we say that Christian myths are equal to other religions or create stats for Jesus, we are offending their beliefs system, not themselves.<br /> <br /> Its like saying most Catholic Priests are pedophile (some evidence point to that), and saying Jesus was gay (some evidence point to that). The first one insults the practitioners of the religion, the second question what they believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-04-2020, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:26:07-07:00","id":1378516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378515#post1378515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but they were in the first case attacking the followers and not the beliefs system and in the second case starting the entire premises that Christian myths are true.<br /> When we say that Christian myths are equal to other religions or create stats for Jesus, we are offending their beliefs system, not themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn\u2019t really that. They were taking Christian beliefs and using them, as myths, to craft original stories with. I mean, \u2018Cain\u2019 is a biblical figure, but his reference point in Vampire is changed to provide a backstory for the game setting. In the words of one Christian reviewer at the time, Vampire was using religious ideas as a \u2018fashion accessory\u2019. So, the point being, it isn\u2019t anything new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:31:39-07:00","id":1378519,"title":"","content":"If I can try to bring this discussion back closer to the original topic, I think that some of the more interesting gods that might come are those who were actual people, like Divus Julius or Confucius.<br /> <br /> I think they are more interesting because they give us a proper view of what is necessary to do in the World to become a god, how big of a deal you have to be to be deified. The one I am particularly interested in is Alexander the Great, which I think is a natural inclusion. What do you all think? Any other interesting people who should be included as a deity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:41:19-07:00","id":1378521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378519#post1378519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can try to bring this discussion back closer to the original topic, I think that some of the more interesting gods that might come are those who were actual people, like Divus Julius or Confucius.<br /> <br /> I think they are more interesting because they give us a proper view of what is necessary to do in the World to become a god, how big of a deal you have to be to be deified. The one I am particularly interested in is Alexander the Great, which I think is a natural inclusion. What do you all think? Any other interesting people who should be included as a deity?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an interesting idea. Another thing I am toying with is creating \u2018Gods\u2019 of a scientific paradigm - so Newton, Maxwell, Einstein type of thing. Not sure if it would work, but you could just focus on historical figures - Napoleon, Julius Caesar, Genghis Khan. Indeed, a lot of leaders like this <i>were</i> deified. Fancy following Caligula?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-04-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:45:28-07:00","id":1378522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378519#post1378519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can try to bring this discussion back closer to the original topic, I think that some of the more interesting gods that might come are those who were actual people, like Divus Julius or Confucius.<br /> <br /> I think they are more interesting because they give us a proper view of what is necessary to do in the World to become a god, how big of a deal you have to be to be deified. The one I am particularly interested in is Alexander the Great, which I think is a natural inclusion. What do you all think? Any other interesting people who should be included as a deity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two are very likely to be Demigods (even the Romans adored Divus Julius as a Demigod, while I don\u2019t know much about Confucius, he would be a chosen Demigod).<br /> The idea that worship create legend makes sense, and probably should be used, but at same time it challenges the need of a patron to ascension, while at same time put The Kardasians somewhere among the demigods (and that\u2019s frightening).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:56:50-07:00","id":1378526,"title":"","content":"It certainly does create an interesting position, that being the nature of divinity itself. Do you need a 'special something' or can enough mortal worship do it? Is mortal worship of any use at all or is it crucial? Is someone like, say, Genghis Khan a god (or a demigod) based on his legend, or is it simply that people have convinced themselves that he <i>must</i> be even though in reality he isn't. What might that mean in either direction? Like, imagine running a campaign where the antagonists (or even the player characters!) are people who seek go obtain divinity and the means in which they go to get it. And, whether, in the end they end up with a bunch of gods going 'Nicely done. Welcome to the gang.' or whether they stand around laughing as the ones who have done so much find that it was all for naught.<br /> <br /> Certainly it might well put the gods into a difficult position in this modern age, with its social media, where dozens, hundreds even, of men and women are being worshipped in such mighty numbers at a time as to suddenly flood the market with nascent deities. And what do the established gods do about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:03:41-07:00","id":1378529,"title":"","content":"While Divus Julius is only mentionned in relation to the nementodevos i think.<br /> Confucius is part of the Shen roster in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:14:51-07:00","id":1378532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378521#post1378521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is an interesting idea. Another thing I am toying with is creating \u2018Gods\u2019 of a scientific paradigm - so Newton, Maxwell, Einstein type of thing. Not sure if it would work, but you could just focus on historical figures - Napoleon, Julius Caesar, Genghis Kahn. Indeed, a lot of leaders like this <i>were</i> deified. Fancy following Caligula?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are already several Gods of the Sciences, Academics and Knowledge, so I'm not sure there's any useful design space the former would be covering even beyond them not being Gods... If you wish to check out a Pantheon with several ascended humans however I strongly suggest <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> Nexus product... it covers the Deities of the Corte Divinas of Maria Lionza, an indigenous religion from Venezuela that includes Gods such as Simon Bolivar and Erik the Red. It is excellently done and a great example of how real religious beliefs continue to evolve and grow to this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:18:04-07:00","id":1378533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378512#post1378512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf games have been offending certain Christian groups since they were founded. Vampire\u2019s lore is based on Christian myths. I doubt it will make any difference here, truth be told.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there was a little game called Demon\u2026<br /> <br /> I know that it can be done wrong, as illustrated in Scion 1e (where the Abrahamic faiths were either the minions of the implicitly malevolent Egyptian Titan or a mortal conspiracy to enslave gods). <br /> <br /> But I don't think that the driving concern is our should be \u201cis there going to be bad publicity if we do this?\u201d For better or worse, Onyx Path and its games aren't going to get the same cultural spotlight that Vampire: the Masquerade got in the 90s. Heck, even by the time that the aforementioned Demon: the Fallen came out in the early 00s, White Wolf's pop culture status was fading, and the supposed Christian backlash against the game existed more within its advertising campaign than in reality. <br /> <br /> No; in this case, \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d has more to do with failing to respect the religion, in the form of insufficient authenticity \u2014 much like Scion 2e has made course corrections on several of the 1e Pantheons in an effort to get the myths right. That said, the same thing that I said in another thread applies here, too: it's entirely possible to be <i>excessively</i> respectful. Scion is a game, and compromises for the sake of playability if nothing else are too be expected. <br /> <br /> It helps that 2e has a better toolkit to work with, most notably Mantles, Primordials, and Chosen Scions. But there's also something about how Pantheons are formed in 2e, with a retconning of the World's history so that their own origin stories become true. This lets you write up each Pantheon on its own terms without having to point out that that's not what \u201c<i>really</i> happened\u201d: all myths are true, even opposing ones; though the latter tends to manifest as inter-Pantheon tensions rather than internal Pantheon inconsistencies (e.g., the Canaanites say one thing; the Abrahamics say another), or possibly through sub-Pantheons. <br /> <br /> Bottom line: I think it's doable, but I appreciate the desire to either do it right or not do it at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:33:40-07:00","id":1378537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378490#post1378490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the best of all possible worlds, I like to imagine each pantheon having its own sourcebook somewhere between the size of Origin and Hero that includes an entire chapter about sorcerers/magicians/whathaveyou in the context of that pantheon's religion, culture and history (as well as ones about supernatural races, terra incognita, divine realms, and so forth). But as is, I'd be ecstatic to see a sorcerers book like what you describe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got a like for that. Ragnarok was good! Oh course the focus will need to change with each pantheon. I could see Scion: Trojan Wars focusing on how the Theoi feud with each other through human conflicts. A Scion: Oracles of the Potter and the Lamb could focus on how the Egyptian gods manipulate and shape their chosen societies. Each pantheon has different goals and needs so each special deep dive book needs to focus on different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:37:32-07:00","id":1378538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378519#post1378519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can try to bring this discussion back closer to the original topic, I think that some of the more interesting gods that might come are those who were actual people, like Divus Julius or Confucius.<br /> <br /> I think they are more interesting because they give us a proper view of what is necessary to do in the World to become a god, how big of a deal you have to be to be deified. The one I am particularly interested in is Alexander the Great, which I think is a natural inclusion. What do you all think? Any other interesting people who should be included as a deity?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot we still don't know in terms of details; but I think that Scion: God 2e may end up borrowing heavily from Mage: the Awakening's supplement Imperial Mysteries: Apotheosis is roughly analogous to what that book calls a Threshold Seeking, where a mage transitions from being an inhabitant of Phenomenal reality who taps into Supernal reality to being am entity who is rooted in Supernal reality and visits Phenomenal reality. There's an appendix called Imperium that talks about the feats one must achieve for the final transformation (which <i>start</i> at Epic) and the effects these changes have on Phenomenal reality. Substitute \u201cWorld\u201d for \u201cPhenomenal reality\u201d and \u201cGod-Realms\u201d for \u201cSupernal Reality\u201d, \u201cdemi-god\u201d for \u201cmage\u201d, \u201cgod\u201d for \u201carchmage\u201d, and \u201cPrimordial\u201d for \u201cAscended Being\u201d, and I suspect you have something that's not too far off from how Scion: God is going to handle matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:38:01-07:00","id":1378539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378472#post1378472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I'd be interested in a supplement for Scion that focuses on sorcerers. Nearly all of the crunch is already there in the form of Motifs and Purviews; so instead of focusing on that side of things, I'd rather see a focus on how one becomes a Sorcerer, coupled with an overview of magical traditions that exist in the World, what they're like, and how they're connected to the Pantheons. Done with the same respect toward the corresponding real-world magical beliefs that Scion has shown toward the religious beliefs that the Pantheons represent. <br /> <br /> In short, Scion really ought to have its own mages, without needing to borrow them from the World or Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, you got a like too. <br /> <br /> A general Sorcerer magic book that makes Socerers playable, gives Scions with a magic theme good tools, introduces the Witch and Mage callings, and gives rules for Socerers to achieve apotheosis, would be grand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T12:40:22-07:00","id":1378600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My objective was pointing the difference between criticizing the practitioners and the belief, not pointing what is true or not (Priests are people like anyone else and suffer form mental issues as anyone, and Jesus, or anyone else, sexuality is not my business).</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid and laudible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T16:14:23-07:00","id":1378627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378522#post1378522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those two are very likely to be Demigods (even the Romans adored Divus Julius as a Demigod, while I don\u2019t know much about Confucius, he would be a chosen Demigod).<br /> The idea that worship create legend makes sense, and probably should be used, but at same time it challenges the need of a patron to ascension, while at same time put The Kardasians somewhere among the demigods (and that\u2019s frightening).</div> </div> </div> </div>Confucius is in the book, and Divus Julius has been announced as a Scion of Venus who became a god, so that is why I choose them as examples of deities who came from mortal ascension.<br /> <br /> Actually, as far as I understand, the number of followers you have has nothing to do with your deification. You don't become a god because many believe in you, but by having so much impact in the world that people recognize you (which isn't the same thing). As is said in the book, having millions of followers on twitter don't give you legend, but gaining legend gives you millions of followers.<br /> <br /> Confucius effectively redefined the Chinese culture, and Julio Caesar conquered a ridiculous amount of land to Rome, arguably destroyed a culture, and took control of the Roman republic. They were big deals, and people recognize them as big deals. Kardashians are famous but will disappear from the culture in a few decades, so I don't think the gods care about media creating gods. Celebrities have existed since the dawn of the time, but unless they can reshape the culture around them, they will just be forgotten when their fans die out.<br /> <br /> People who were a big deal that come into my mind that could have become gods: Alexander the Great, who altered the culture of everything from Macedonia to Pakistan, and reshaped Egyptian rule. Imhotep supposedly created a few staples of the Ancient Egyptian culture, if I am not mistaken. Ghengis Khan, who reshaped Asian political structure. Karl Marx could too, as his Manifesto reshaped the World. Bonaparte sounds more like a failed demigod to me, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T18:58:48-07:00","id":1378651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378627#post1378627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Confucius is in the book, and Divus Julius has been announced as a Scion of Venus who became a god, so that is why I choose them as examples of deities who came from mortal ascension.<br /> <br /> Actually, as far as I understand, the number of followers you have has nothing to do with your deification. You don't become a god because many believe in you, but by having so much impact in the world that people recognize you (which isn't the same thing). As is said in the book, having millions of followers on twitter don't give you legend, but gaining legend gives you millions of followers.<br /> <br /> Confucius effectively redefined the Chinese culture, and Julio Caesar conquered a ridiculous amount of land to Rome, arguably destroyed a culture, and took control of the Roman republic. They were big deals, and people recognize them as big deals. Kardashians are famous but will disappear from the culture in a few decades, so I don't think the gods care about media creating gods. Celebrities have existed since the dawn of the time, but unless they can reshape the culture around them, they will just be forgotten when their fans die out.<br /> <br /> People who were a big deal that come into my mind that could have become gods: Alexander the Great, who altered the culture of everything from Macedonia to Pakistan, and reshaped Egyptian rule. Imhotep supposedly created a few staples of the Ancient Egyptian culture, if I am not mistaken. Ghengis Khan, who reshaped Asian political structure. Karl Marx could too, as his Manifesto reshaped the World. Bonaparte sounds more like a failed demigod to me, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few celebrities might make it to godhood. Author celebrities like Shakespeare or Shelley might make it. Twain, Dickens, Poe, Tolstoy, Zola, and similar authors might make it. Of media celebrities only Charlie Chaplin, Elvis, Humphrey Bogart, John Wayne, the Beatles, Greta Garbo, and Marylin Monroe, have the kind of sustained impact to make it. I could really only see the Beatles, because of their mystical influences making it.<br /> <br /> Of the author celebrities, a higher number might make it because of sustained Influence. I could see Ursula Le Guin and Harlan Ellison waking up shocked to see they have a shot at apotheosis. ;-) The lady would have the wittier comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-04-2020, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:11:29-07:00","id":1378652,"title":"","content":"It's depends on whether you need to be a demigod before you can be a god. And whether you need to be a hero before you can be a demigod. And whether or not you need some sort of Divine assistance to become a hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:43:32-07:00","id":1378659,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that some sort of Heroes of History thing, looking at certain famous dead people<sup>1</sup> in the context of them being Scion Hero characters/NPCs would be a really cool Storypath Nexus product. <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>I'd never consider using living people as you never know when you might run into the Cosby Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T23:06:29-07:00","id":1378683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storypath Nexus </div> </div> </div>I'd like to aggressively recommend this. It's great that people have their own ideas on who should and shouldn't be included. But what I'd suggest is that instead of begging other people to do the work for you, make some time, do the research, get as much feedback as you can, and put it out there yourself. That's what the Nexus is for.<br /> <br /> The writers for OPP aren't magical special people with exclusive access to knowledge. They might be a little more experienced at doing research and developing academic contacts, but probably not by some wide margin, and it's something you yourself can learn to do. Figure out who knows stuff, get multiple opinions and cross-reference them. Read the original texts yourself as best as you can. Then do up your own take. Support others doing their takes, too.<br /> <br /> If you believe in your idea, make it real yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T23:41:54-07:00","id":1378687,"title":"","content":"If I was to do one (and for me the biggest issue is probably formatting/layout and art), I'd probably do three people, Miyamoto Musashi, Rani Velu Nachiyar, and Davy Crockett. And if it went over well enough, a second one with Cleopatra, El Santo, and Lord Byron or Leonardo da Vinci.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T04:03:31-07:00","id":1378718,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> There\u2019s a book called Three Roads to the Alamo, about Davy Crockett (he HATED that name, his political enemies made it up to make fun of him; he preferred to be called David) and two other heroes of the Alamo (Jim Bowie and Colonel William Travis). It\u2019s a really good book (among other things, there\u2019s a two page discussion about whether William Travis really banged 56 girls). Anyway, the final chapter of the book, where it talks about Davy Crockett\u2019s death at the Alamo, is called \u201cApotheosis.\u201d Not even kidding. He\u2019d make a great Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T09:35:41-07:00","id":1378778,"title":"","content":"How did that go again? \u201cIf you surrender now, I'll put in a good word for you with my friend Sam. I can't guarantee anything, mind you; he's got a bit of a temper. But I'll try.\u201d Or something like that. Almost certainly apocryphal. Also very definitely legendary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T10:37:30-07:00","id":1378792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378652#post1378652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's depends on whether you need to be a demigod before you can be a god. And whether you need to be a hero before you can be a demigod. And whether or not you need some sort of Divine assistance to become a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it seems the Celestial Bureaucracy straight picks up ghosts and hands them the Godbadge, do not pass go do not collect two hundred dollars.<br /> <br /> So its safe to talk about nongods as god options now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So would mortals becoming gods due to being influential or revolutionary need pantheon sponsorship, as in they can't become it as a consequence of being S-M-R-T? If that is the case I really see something maybe like a Celestial court of law where they have the best divine debaters and lawspeakers arguing about who gets sign up who into their pantheon. It would be like how sportsteams target college players mixed with patent and copyright lawyers in court.<br /> <br /> <br /> But unless I have a different idea for a specific game I have Daedalus patronized by Hephaestus and through him trying to recruit revolutionary big brains like Leonardo Da Vinci and Nikola Tesla. I would have them raise through the ranks of Demigod and then Godhood then. How I bet the Celestial Bureaucracy handles it is more like they recruit some in a position of Demigod level immortal (I have it Guanyu had his Oath Brothers of Liu Bei and Zhang Fei raised as Demigods early on as a favor as Guanyu was starting out as a God) and then they shanghaied Confucius and Laotzu into full blown godhood due to cultural importance and their legacy to the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T12:33:58-07:00","id":1378826,"title":"","content":"In actual Greek myth a shepherd fishing for his dinner put fish on a patch of grass while he caught some more fish. The fish came back to life and jumped into the sea. The shepherd was dumbfounded and tried tasting the grass. This caused him to jump into the sea as well and the waters of the sea made him into a god. I'll look him up later, but this god goes back to the time of Homer at least.<br /> <br /> So people becoming gods just because is a thing in at least classical myth.<br /> <br /> The god was Glaucus, he was worshiped by sailors, he was prayed to for protection at sea and seems to have inspired good seamanship.<br /> <br /> His callings would be ...<br /> <br /> Guardian: He protects Fishermen and sailors.<br /> <br /> Sage: He advises Fishermen and sailors and teaches them useful skills and caution.<br /> <br /> Lover: His myths revolve around either his love for the nymph Scylla or the God Melicertes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-05-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T13:40:45-07:00","id":1378835,"title":"","content":"That's true. But this isn't classical myth; it's Scion. And it does some things differently. For instance, there are other Pantheons who remember the Theoi from before they achieved godhood. Yep; in Scion, even Zeus started out as a Hero and worked his way up to divinity. (I suspect that when the Theoi achieved Pantheon status, the history of the World was rewritten so that Zeus was always a god; but that's the World, not the God-realms: the Theoi don't get to rewrite what the Netjer remember.) Scion simply doesn't have \u201cI was born as a god, and was never anything else.\u201d<br /> <br /> So the fact that there isn't a \u201cjust because\u201d Origin strongly implies that there are no \u201cjust because\u201d gods. You are, of course, free to house rule that; but as far as I can tell, that <i>would</i> be a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-05-2020, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:26:37-07:00","id":1378877,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T17:47:25-07:00","id":1378888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378835#post1378835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true. But this isn't classical myth; it's Scion. And it does some things differently. For instance, there are other Pantheons who remember the Theoi from before they achieved godhood. Yep; in Scion, even Zeus started out as a Hero and worked his way up to divinity. (I suspect that when the Theoi achieved Pantheon status, the history of the World was rewritten so that Zeus was always a god; but that's the World, not the God-realms: the Theoi don't get to rewrite what the Netjer remember.) Scion simply doesn't have \u201cI was born as a god, and was never anything else.\u201d<br /> <br /> So the fact that there isn't a \u201cjust because\u201d Origin strongly implies that there are no \u201cjust because\u201d gods. You are, of course, free to house rule that; but as far as I can tell, that <i>would</i> be a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's pre-Classical. It is contemporary with Homer because it's referenced in poetry from that time period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T18:12:57-07:00","id":1378892,"title":"","content":"The point remains the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T02:20:26-07:00","id":1379434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378371#post1378371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have one I wrote up ages ago for free <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Ganga, Whose Waters Cleanse the Worlds</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <b>Aliases:</b> Bhagirathi, Alaknanda, Surtarangini<br /> <br /> Praise be to Ganga, Goddess of the sacred waters that flow through the realms of Deva, Human and Asura alike. When Vishnu in his Dwarf Incarnation raised his foot to cover all Heaven, his toe pierced the Primordial Waters, and a stream shot forth, bathing his feet, before being collected by Brahma in his water-pot. This selfsame stream is Ganga, daughter of the Himalaya Mountains and sister to Parvati.<br /> <br /> Bhagiratha, Scion of Shiva, born through his blessing to two Queens, sought to bring Ganga down to Earth, as a means of salvation for his cursed ancestors. Pleased with his austerities, Brahma tipped over his water-pot, and Ganga raced towards the World; but in her arrogance, Ganga thought to smash through the ground. Fearing that he had doomed humanity, Bhagiratha invoked Shiva, who answered his call. Shiva stood at the point of impact, and caught Ganga up in his matted locks, before letting her loose in a controlled stream. Bhagiratha then worshipped her and explained his mission, to help all humanity with her waters.<br /> <br /> This experience changed Ganga, who took Bhagirath's name as one of her own; she spread her waters out into all realms of existence, existing as a river in Heaven Earth and Hell, and other regions besides, and now dedicates herself to the salvation of Deva, Human and Asura alike. Like Ganesha, she is an advocate of peace, and her many children usually inherit their mother's altruistic streak. With King Santanu, Ganga bore the mightiest of Born Deva Scions, Bheeshma of the Mahabharata. She often takes an active role in her Scions' development, and they likewise spearhead efforts to purify her sacred river. Still, some of them fear that they will never live up to their most famous sibling.<br /> <br /> <i>Callings:</i><br /> \u2022 <i>Healer:</i> Strongly associated with purification and the salvation of souls<br /> \u2022 <i>Liminal:</i> Her flows exist in multiple realms simultaneously, capable of releasing souls and sending them to their next destination<br /> \u2022 <i>Lover:</i> Seduces King Santanu, is often linked to multiple Gods with no clear consensus on a husband<br /> <br /> Purviews:<br /> \u2022 <i>Fertility:</i> Mother Goddess prayed to for fertile fields, considered spiritual mother by many along her banks<br /> \u2022 <i>Journeys:</i> Moves between Worlds with ease, her waters allow passage to other Terrae<br /> \u2022 <i>Water:</i> Most famous of the river Goddesses of India</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea! I think the God of the Himalayas would be interesting Giri-Raj/Himavat! Especially because of its site as a pilgrimage to multiple religions.<br /> <br /> Wasn't their mention of the Pali Pantheon in the Core? I want to say it was in the Guanyin Avalokitesvara connection, man I remember having to do papers on that God in Uni.<br /> <br /> But this makes me think about the Nature of the personification of Sumeru. Mount Meru is personified to make a child which is the Wife of Himavat. Meru is also unspeakably huge, so it could actually maybe be a Titan/Primordial rather then a god? Thoughts on this? I really would love a book that covers the Devas connection to the Pali pantheon, and the Pre-Vedic Gods. Pre-Shiva Rudra clearly had some aspects, like his title, taken and absorbed by Shiva if Rudra isn't actually an aspect of Shiva. But the Devas seem like they connect to the most Pantheons, well maybe the Greek may have beaten them on spreading farthest, what with the Buddhist Hercules statues to act as a sacred guardian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:29:35-07:00","id":1379599,"title":"","content":"Considering I am a New Zealander, I ought to ask if there have been any Polynesian/Maori Pantheons made just yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:33:15-07:00","id":1379603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1379599#post1379599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering I am a New Zealander, I ought to ask if there have been any Polynesian/Maori Pantheons made just yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Polynesian Confederation Pantheon slated for Demigod. I think that most of it is Maori-influenced but it will also have room for some other Pacific Islander Gods.<br /> <br /> The writer behind it is Mendez, who also wrote the Deva, the Orisha, and the Shen in the Hero book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:54:50-07:00","id":1379618,"title":"","content":"Cool. There are plenty of resources on the web about Maori gods, including wikipedia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:M\u0101ori_gods\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:M\u0101ori_gods</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:53:16-07:00","id":1379694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1378342#post1378342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dispute this, you will punish me for disputing this. There is no method of disputing moderation when moderators handle the complaints. I've pointed out disagreements with you in the past and my opinion of you misusing your power because you have an arbitrary grudge. You will ban me and there will be no consequence to your history of behavior.<br /> <br /> I was responding to someone's response that I interpreted as they don't respect anyone who disagrees with them. The starter of the conversation even rebutted with validation for my opinion.<br /> <br /> Once again Lioness In my opinion is going to abuse their power to pursue a grudge. There is no mediation or a system for pursuing redress. Civility was upheld even in this very post I am making.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Sorry, I was otherwise occupied but have reviewed both posts, it's clearly a rules violation and you know better, man. Doubling down by backtalking on just a warning? 30 day suspension. There's a system for lodging complaints and you know what it is, the link is in the Forum Terms of Use and at the bottom of my sig.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 04-09-2020, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:03:43-07:00","id":1379738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1379599#post1379599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering I am a New Zealander, I ought to ask if there have been any Polynesian/Maori Pantheons made just yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to my knowledge, but there's a ton of good data out there, so it's only a matter of time. Why don't you give it a go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T07:32:47-07:00","id":1379758,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it would work to have Maori and Hawaiian (and other) pantheons that are tied together similarly to the way the Orisha and Loa are. <br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that a Finnish pantheon would be cool. They have a lot of interesting ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T08:12:10-07:00","id":1379764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1379758#post1379758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it would work to have Maori and Hawaiian (and other) pantheons that are tied together similarly to the way the Orisha and Loa are.<br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that a Finnish pantheon would be cool. They have a lot of interesting ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to the first question is yes. I assume many pantheons would share gods.<br /> <br /> And you get a like for suggesting the Finns. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:38:12-07:00","id":1379930,"title":"","content":"Rumors I've heard Here and There seem to imply that... To call the Atua (the Polynesian 'Pantheon' slated for Demigod <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1379603#post1379603\">I mentioned here</a>) a unified Pantheon isn't really accurate <i>persay</i>, as while certain names crop up across multiple islands, sometimes they can be with different contexts. Mantles provide a handwave for how the same Godly Figure may we worshipped with different connotations between cultures.<br /> <br /> It's kind of more a Confederation of Semi-Shared Divine Figures. Given who's writing it for Demigod, I figure it may not be entirely unlike this hypothetical snippet I just made up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maui is even credited with stealing Fire from beneath the earth to give to humanity. Who EXACTLY he stole fire from varies from island to island, and frankly, Maui is happy to take credit for all of them. </div> </div> </div>Granted I'm mostly guessing based on Mendez's write-ups for the Deva, where each God has somewhere between two and fifteen origins.<br /> <br /> Edit: And while I myself am not well-versed enough to make any of them, I wager someone who does sufficient studying could probably make a Maori- or Hawaiian-specific Sub Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Edit2: I also know someone who would love nothing more than to make a bunch of Pacific Island Pantheons, ESPECIALLY Hawaiian, as he loves Hawaiian mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-10-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:37:52-07:00","id":1380236,"title":"","content":"I would like to see Zhu Rong.<br /> I would also like to see write ups for the seven immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T02:11:04-07:00","id":1380338,"title":"","content":"Well, now I'm excited for the Atua! Mendez' pantheons all happen to be my favourites in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1380236#post1380236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see Zhu Rong.<br /> I would also like to see write ups for the seven immortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this. Personally, I feel like the Sh\u00e9n are still missing the most major deities out of all the pantheons we have so far. I would love to see gods like Mazu, Xuanwu, Wenchang Wang, Houtu, Tudigong, Zao Shen, Zhong Kui,... Let's hope they eventually get to make expansions focusing on the individual pantheons!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":25842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","user":"Mr Wopsle","date":". 04-11-2020, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:16:54-07:00","id":1381160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods#post1378119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says on the tin. Gods that we want to see show up later.<br /> <br /> I'm glad the Loa are promised. The Baron was particularly missed.<br /> <br /> For the Theoi four stand out. Hercules, who had more temples in ancient Greece/Hellas than several of the standard twelve and was a major deity in ancient times. Hecate, again a major figure. Iris, also a messenger of the gods. And the Roman god Mars, who is nothing like Ares. In fact Ares was rarely worshiped in Greece and Mars was a major figure in Rome. Ares was the god of battle lust and Mars was the god of adult male social roles. For early Rome these were Farmer, Solider, Priest, and husband/lover. The Solider role got overemphasized in the later empire.<br /> <br /> For the Tuatha, certain figured associated with their pantheon like Oberon and Mab who aren't true members but connected would be good.<br /> <br /> More as I think of them.<br /> <br /> Who do you want to show up later?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that some of my old favorites didn't show up. I was strangely fond of Tlazlteotl. That is why they put Emanuel Montero as a sample character. He is a Scion of Xiuhtecutli, who does not appear in the books. They point out that if you want to be a Scion of, say, Baron Samedi, you just have choose a single Calling and Purview. The Cheval/Gun Purview is actually stated to belong to both the Orisha and the Loa.<br /> <br /> This allows us to play our forgotten friends from 1st edition, lets mythological scholars use their favorite obscure dieties, and creepy teenage boys can make Scions of Priapus.<br /> <br /> Brian<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/243-billionsix","name":"BillionSix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:43:45-07:00","id":1381169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BillionSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1381160#post1381160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that some of my old favorites didn't show up. I was strangely fond of Tlazlteotl. That is why they put Emanuel Montero as a sample character. He is a Scion of Xiuhtecutli, who does not appear in the books. They point out that if you want to be a Scion of, say, Baron Samedi, you just have choose a single Calling and Purview. The Cheval/Gun Purview is actually stated to belong to both the Orisha and the Loa.<br /> <br /> This allows us to play our forgotten friends from 1st edition, lets mythological scholars use their favorite obscure dieties, and creepy teenage boys can make Scions of Priapus.<br /> <br /> Brian<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't give them ideas. Of course Priapus is actually interesting. He was a protective deity who scared evil spirits away. Only I don't see creepy boys being protective and calming. (Sigh)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T13:41:50-07:00","id":1381760,"title":"","content":"That reminds me, I was kind of sad to see Tlazolteotl absent from the Aztec pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T18:17:42-07:00","id":1381836,"title":"","content":"A note on deities shared between pantheons in places like the Polynesian and North America would be useful. Especially with worked examples and notes on how to follow in the footsteps of such beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T03:21:02-07:00","id":1381882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1381760#post1381760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, I was kind of sad to see Tlazolteotl absent from the Aztec pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go, a quick statting of her from the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Tlazolteotl:<br /> Callings:<br /> Creator: Mother Goddess, conflated with Teteo Innan, &quot;Mother of [All] the Gods&quot;.<br /> Healer: Goddess of the steam bath, of midwives/female doctors, remover of sin.<br /> Judge: Goddess of sin and its punishment, brings ill luck to sinners.<br /> <br /> Purviews:<br /> Artistry (Weaving): Closely associated with this prime female skill, wears spindles in her hair.<br /> Earth: Conflated with Tonantzin, the earth mother, her steam bath is the womb of the earth, sin is represented as dirt.<br /> Fertility: Associated both with human sexuality/fertility and with the cotton plant.<br /> Fortune: Brings ill luck to sinners.<br /> Health: Goddess of the steam bath, of midwives/female doctors, inflicts illness as punishment and removes it again.<br /> Passion (Lust): Associated with human sexuality and prostitution, inspires the sexual sins she punishes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T16:15:21-07:00","id":1382006,"title":"","content":"Could there be forgotten Gods? That is, pantheons that have been lost to history, either by conquest or disaster, that are seeking to make a comeback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T16:29:19-07:00","id":1382008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1382006#post1382006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could there be forgotten Gods? That is, pantheons that have been lost to history, either by conquest or disaster, that are seeking to make a comeback?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean part of it is like... What do you write when we know nothing? Like with the Atlantis Pantheon that's going to be in the Companion, sure, make it all up because Atlantis never existed.<br /> <br /> There's design space for God's who are more forgotten, the claiming of a Mantle that hasn't been worshipped for some time. But I, personally, wouldn't put a real-life culture's name on a Pantheon I pulled right out of my butt. Might as well go the extra mile and just make up a culture of my own creation to go with the Gods I made up.<br /> <br /> Edit: Plus, arguably, we're getting that kind of thing with the Nemetondevos in the Companion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T22:14:51-07:00","id":1382062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1381836#post1381836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A note on deities shared between pantheons in places like the Polynesian and North America would be useful. Especially with worked examples and notes on how to follow in the footsteps of such beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I appreciate about Scion is the fact that they didn't name the Pantheons based on geography or ethnic group, but rather called them by a general descriptor that the member gods themselves might use. It's not &quot;The Indian Pantheon&quot;. It's &quot;The Deva of South Asia&quot;. It's kinda like, oh, &quot;The People&quot; isn't such a helpful term now that we know there's an entire globe out there, but we can still name ourselves and specify where we mostly came from.<br /> <br /> The unifying feature of a Pantheon is much less, &quot;so this one group of people worshipped them,&quot; but rather &quot;We've got a Signature Purview that our stories tend to suggest we're preoccupied with and here are two Virtues that our stories tend to have opinions about and also mildly contradict each other enough to be character hooks.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T19:10:49-08:00","id":1547404,"title":"","content":"Some pantheons are known vaguely and from the outside, the Telchines the preclassical deities of Rhodes. In variant Greek myths, they raised Poseidon. (Yes I know that contradics the legend of Kronos eating his children. Many myths we accept as standard are only the literary choice, not the actual popular favorites). They were said to be magicians and smiths. In another replay of the Titans and Giants, the Telchines, long allies of Olympus, revoted and were conquered. <br /> <br /> They'd make interesting defeated and bitter foes of the Theoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T22:37:59-08:00","id":1547443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1547404#post1547404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some pantheons are known vaguely and from the outside, the Telchines the preclassical deities of Rhodes. In variant Greek myths, they raised Poseidon. (Yes I know that contradics the legend of Kronos eating his children. Many myths we accept as standard are only the literary choice, not the actual popular favorites). They were said to be magicians and smiths. In another replay of the Titans and Giants, the Telchines, long allies of Olympus, revoted and were conquered.<br /> <br /> They'd make interesting defeated and bitter foes of the Theoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were the Telechines gods though? I always thought they were monsters from the age of the (Greek) Titans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28702-xanah","name":"Xanah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28702_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T11:48:34-08:00","id":1547461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1378119-missing-gods?p=1547443#post1547443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were the Telechines gods though? I always thought they were monsters from the age of the (Greek) Titans</div> </div> </div> </div>The evidence is that the people of the island of Rhodes worshiped the Telchines as gods in the pre classical period. The Olympians seemed to have replaced the Telchines, at least among the upper classes, before Roman times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}